==============================================================================
(1) AT DEGENERACY EVERY DELIVERY LAW AGREES — THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT
==============================================================================
  Stage 1 has eps_q = a for every q, so w_q = w for every q. Any transfer weight is a
  function of w alone, so it returns the SAME number for all three modes:

  transfer weight                                E_neutral   E_charged   equal?
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  sudden, 1/w^2 per mode   (the corpus's pin)     1.000000    1.000000      YES
  flat per log                                    1.000000    1.000000      YES
  thermal / equipartition                         1.000000    1.000000      YES
  resonant, 1/w                                   1.000000    1.000000      YES
  anything else f(w)                              1.367879    1.367879      YES

  Trivially true and load-bearing: the delivery-law ambiguity that has cost this arc
  three cycles simply does not exist while the modes are degenerate. Equal energy at a
  common frequency is equal quanta, so the pour hands over a common occupation number
  no matter how impulsive it is.

==============================================================================
(2) ORDER A — POUR FIRST, THEN SPLIT ADIABATICALLY
==============================================================================
  The pour lands on degenerate modes (common n), then the face-face bonds ramp on and
  each mode conserves its action, so n is carried through unchanged. At the end
  <x^2> = (2n+1) hbar / (2 M w) with a COMMON n:

    <x^2>_neutral ~ 1/w_0 = 1.00000000
    <x^2>_charged ~ 1/w_1 = 0.50000000
    R^2/f_0^2 = 1.00000000      (the null needs 1)
    Q = 0.6666666667      (2/3 = 0.6666666667)
    miss = 0.000 ppm

==============================================================================
(3) ORDER B — SPLIT FIRST, THEN THE SUDDEN POUR
==============================================================================
  Now the pour arrives on an already-split spectrum and its w-dependence bites. With the
  pinned sudden weight E_q ~ 1/w_q^2, and <x^2> = E/(M w^2), the amplitude goes as 1/w^4:

    <x^2>_neutral ~ 1/w_0^4 = 1.00000000
    <x^2>_charged ~ 1/w_1^4 = 0.06250000
    R^2/f_0^2 = 0.12500000      (the null needs 1)
    Q = 0.3750000000      (2/3 = 0.6666666667)
    miss = 43.8%

  and the stiffness ratio that WOULD make order B work is not 4:
    R^2/f_0^2 = 2 (w_0/w_1)^4 = 2 (eps_0/eps_1)^2 = 1  ->  eps_1/eps_0 = sqrt2
    check: 2*(1/math.sqrt(2))**2 = 1.0000000000
  which is neither the graph's 4 nor the thermal 2 nor the ring-on-ring 1/2.

==============================================================================
(4) THE TWO ORDERS ARE NOT CLOSE, SO THIS IS A REAL PREDICTION
==============================================================================
  order                                           Q       from 2/3
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  A: pour while degenerate, then split   0.6666666667       0.000 ppm
  B: split first, then sudden pour     0.3750000000         43.8 %

  Order B misses by 44% -- it is not a near-miss to be fixed by a
  correction. The mechanism therefore does not merely tolerate an ordering, it REQUIRES
  one, and says which.

==============================================================================
(5) IS ORDER A THE ONE THE CORPUS ALREADY PINS?
==============================================================================
  It is what the corpus's own words describe, though the corpus has not drawn the
  consequence. Pin 2 calls the pour 'genesis, one instant' -- an injection event. The
  face-face couplings are what the medium MEDIATES between faces, so they cannot precede
  the faces' existence as excitations of that medium (P4a). Injection into the newborn,
  still-degenerate ring, followed by the ring's own structure developing, is order A.

  WHAT WOULD REFUTE IT. If the corpus's freeze dynamics place the face-face coupling as
  present from the first instant -- i.e. the ring is born already split -- then order B
  applies, the mechanism predicts Q = 0.375, and it is dead. That is a clean kill
  condition on a structural question, not on a measurement.

  WHAT IS NO LONGER OWED. The 'delivery law at freeze' fork does not need settling in
  the form it was posed. It only mattered because the sectors were assumed split when
  the energy arrived. Under order A every law gives the same answer, so the question
  collapses from 'which weight' to 'which order' -- and the second is answerable from
  structure rather than from a rate nobody has measured.

  STILL OWED, and smaller than before: (P4b)'s adiabaticity is now needed only for the
  SPLIT, not for the pour. The pour may be as impulsive as the corpus pins it.
